   "text": {
    "L1": "Our land has had many names over time, and those names tell us about its past.",
    "L2": "Bharata was used by people of the land and is linked to the Bharata clan in the Rig Veda.",
    "L3": "Jambudvipa means the land of the jambu, or jamun, tree. It appears in old texts and an inscription of Ashoka.",
    "L4": "Now watch the word chain from the river Sindhu to the name India.",
    "L5": "Persians pronounced the s in Sindhu as h, saying Hindu. Greeks changed this to Indos, and Indos led to India.",
    "L6": "So India was not invented recently by the British; it is a name shaped through older languages and travellers.",
    "L7": "The Constitution gives both names: India, that is Bharat, shall be a Union of States.",
    "L8": "India and Bharat are two official names for the same country. Now choose the correct statement."
   },
